The [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix queued. Its own table says
otherwise once it renders: the reports merged into it do not share one cause. This page splits
them by cause and gives each cause a ticket of its own.

## What #4471 holds

The desk's own view of #4471, built from its data at render time:

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## The tickets

One ticket per cause in #4471, counted as the table above counts them:

- `parser`, the shared parser reads a day-first date month first:
  [frimoldi/mega-what-it-shows#1](https://github.com/frimoldi/mega-what-it-shows/issues/1)
- `hint`, the booking-v3 form hints `MM/DD/YYYY`, then reads the date day first:
  [frimoldi/mega-what-it-shows#2](https://github.com/frimoldi/mega-what-it-shows/issues/2)

## How a report is placed

- **parser**: the tenant writes the day first, and the report did not come through the
  booking-v3 form. The shared parser reads the date month first, so day and month swap. The
  queued fix for #4471 is this one.
- **hint**: the tenant runs booking-v3 and the report came through its form. The form prints
  `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field, people type month first as it tells them, and the form
  reads the date the tenant's way, day first. The parser fix does not touch this: the hint has
  to follow the tenant's locale.

The footnote under the table: the desk read a few `parser` reports as a one-day move
(`desk-notes.json`). It files and counts them under `parser` by tenant, so they are in #1, which
names them. Their bodies describe a date one day off rather than a day/month swap: check them
again when the parser fix ships.

The cause comes from the tenant (`locales.ts`), not from the intake tag. Intake guesses from
the reporter's browser, and on #4471 it is wrong in both directions: see the "tagged as"
column on the [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471).

## Why they were merged

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on the subject line alone. The
subjects in #4471, such as "Date is wrong" and "Wrong day on the invite", fit every one of
these problems, so they all landed in one ticket. The [triage page](/kb/triage/dedupe) that applies
the rule is marked stale.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is marked known, with one fix queued. That fix covers the parser problem only. The hint
problem stays open until its own ticket closes.
</Callout>

## What the desk does now

- Keep #4471 for the parser problem: the queued fix covers it.
- Send new reports from the booking-v3 form to the hint ticket.
- Count each report once, by id: the export repeats some.

